---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.jsx";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.jsx";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Experiments | The Build Room | Ashleigh Magloire"
  description="A full-stack HR support assistant MVP exploring deterministic mock AI classification and human-reviewed response drafts."
>
  <Navbar client:load />

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[var(--portfolio-bg)] text-[var(--portfolio-ink)]">
    <div class="px-6 pt-8 md:px-10 md:pt-10">
      <a
        href="/the-build-room"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--portfolio-accent)] transition hover:text-[var(--portfolio-ink)]"
      >
        <span aria-hidden="true">←</span>
        Back to The Build Room
      </a>
    </div>

    <section class="border-b border-[var(--portfolio-line)] px-6 pb-12 pt-8 md:px-10 md:pb-16 md:pt-10">
      <div class="grid w-full gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] lg:items-end">
        <div>
          <p class="mb-5 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-[var(--portfolio-accent)]">
            The Build Room / Experiments
          </p>

          <h1 class="max-w-4xl font-serif text-4xl leading-tight text-[var(--portfolio-ink)] md:text-6xl">
            Questions I’m working through in code.
          </h1>
        </div>

        <p class="min-h-14 max-w-xl text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)] md:text-base">
          Each one is a small, focused trial, with notes on what worked, what
          didn’t and what I’d do differently.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="px-6 py-10 md:px-10 md:py-14" aria-label="Experiments">
      <div class="mb-5 flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-end gap-3 border-b border-[var(--portfolio-line)] pb-4">
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
          <span class="font-serif text-2xl text-[var(--portfolio-ink)]"> 1 </span>
          experiment
        </p>
      </div>

      <article class="rounded-xl border border-[var(--portfolio-line)] bg-[var(--portfolio-surface)] p-5 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
          <p class="w-fit rounded-full bg-[#F2E2D2] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-[#754D2E]">
            MVP experiment
          </p>

          <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
            React · FastAPI · PostgreSQL
          </p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="mt-5 font-serif text-3xl text-[var(--portfolio-ink)] md:text-4xl">
          HR Management Platform
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)] md:text-base">
          How can a support workflow organise incoming HR requests while
          keeping classification and response suggestions reviewable by people?
        </p>

        <div class="mt-7 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr_auto_1fr] md:items-stretch">
          <section class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--portfolio-line)] bg-[var(--portfolio-bg)] p-4">
            <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
              Frontend
            </p>

            <h3 class="mt-3 font-medium">Employee submits a demo request</h3>

            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
              The React and TypeScript interface collects the request and shows
              the submitted ticket in the employee demo view.
            </p>
          </section>

          <div class="hidden items-center justify-center text-xl text-[var(--portfolio-accent)] md:flex" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </div>

          <section class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--portfolio-line)] bg-[var(--portfolio-bg)] p-4">
            <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
              Backend
            </p>

            <h3 class="mt-3 font-medium">FastAPI classifies the ticket</h3>

            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
              FastAPI validates and stores the request. Deterministic mock logic
              returns a category, priority, suggested response and reasoning.
            </p>
          </section>

          <div class="hidden items-center justify-center text-xl text-[var(--portfolio-accent)] md:flex" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </div>

          <section class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--portfolio-line)] bg-[var(--portfolio-bg)] p-4">
            <p class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
              Review
            </p>

            <h3 class="mt-3 font-medium">HR or Admin reviews the suggestion</h3>

            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
              Demo review queues display the ticket and suggested response.
              A person remains responsible for deciding what to do.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>

        <section class="mt-7 border-t border-[var(--portfolio-line)] pt-6">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--portfolio-ink)]">
            What the MVP demonstrates
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-2 max-w-4xl text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
            The project connects a React and TypeScript frontend to a FastAPI
            backend and PostgreSQL database. Its demo views support ticket
            submission, mock classification, suggested response drafts,
            filtering, sorting and ticket status updates.
          </p>
        </section>

        <details class="group mt-6 border-t border-[var(--portfolio-line)] pt-5">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--portfolio-ink)]">
            <span>What worked, what’s limited, and what I’d do next</span>
            <span class="text-xl transition group-open:rotate-45" aria-hidden="true">
              +
            </span>
          </summary>

          <div class="mt-5 grid gap-5 border-l-2 border-[#B8794F] pl-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <section>
              <h3 class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--portfolio-accent)]">
                What worked
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
                Deterministic keyword rules make the mock classification
                predictable and runnable locally without API keys or external
                AI services. Returning the reasoning alongside the category,
                priority and draft makes the suggestion easier to review.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h3 class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--portfolio-accent)]">
                Current limitations
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
                Keyword matching is limited and is not a real language model.
                The Employee, HR Team and Admin views are demos; real
                authentication and role-based access are not implemented.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h3 class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[var(--portfolio-accent)]">
                What I’d do next
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--portfolio-muted)]">
                Expand backend tests for classification edge cases, add
                authentication and role-based access, and improve the review
                queues. Any future LLM integration would need validated
                structured output and a mock fallback.
              </p>
            </section>
          </div>
        </details>

        <aside class="mt-6 rounded-lg border border-[#D8B69D] bg-[#F8F0E9] p-4">
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#533B2B]">
            Demo data only
          </h3>

          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-[#654E3F]">
            This project is not intended for real employee, HR, medical, payroll
            or other sensitive workplace information. Classification and
            response outputs are draft suggestions, not automatic decisions.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</MainLayout>